WEBVTT

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.440
I-I don’t believe it!

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.990
It’s true!

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:10.830
Since Panda-chan’s dough explodes
multiple times, the bread is really fluffy.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.950
It feels like you’re eating cotton candy.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.500
After it’s exploded once,
a hole opens up in the dough.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.590
Once there’s a hole,
it can’t possibly explode again!

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.300
Just like a balloon.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:27.050
So... it’s impossible to make
it explode two or three times!

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.140
There isn’t much point in saying that.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.510
I saw it with my very own eyes.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.390
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.310
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.560
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.980
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.280
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.870
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.590
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:12.760
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:27.860
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:36.450
probably helped me notice that

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:42.370
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:51.220
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.590
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:03.730
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:09.520
that white sky with my colors.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:16.530
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.910
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.450
The miraculous steamed bread!!

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.660
The day Panda became a panda!

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:37.340
Very well then, we will now start the
seventh match of Yakitate!! 9, here in Gero.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.100
Begin!

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.190
Will Azuma be... all right?

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.400
An Alps steamed bread that
explodes over and over again.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.160
If there really is a technique to make something
like that, then our opponent is undefeatable!

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.950
Wh-What’s with Azuma’s dough?!

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.790
It’s expanded like he already had it ready from earlier.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.460
He made the dough in advance?

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:03.790
Isn’t that against the rules?

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.500
It is not against the rules.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.170
I have already approved this matter.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.170
There is nothing describing any impropriety in bringing in pre-made dough

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.680
in this show’s rule book.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.260
Also...

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:20.020
His opponent, Panda, has also
brought in pre-made baking powder.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.680
So, the conditions are equal.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.140
I see...

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.690
No problems, then.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:29.650
But... I wonder what kind of trick he
has applied to that pre-made dough...?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.150
That is...

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.240
dough made in the Roumen style.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.230
Manager!

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.230
Ken-ken!

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:40.870
Sorry I’m late. I got stuck in a little dispute of theirs.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.160
B-But you’re hurt!

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.450
These are bullet holes, right? Right?

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.450
They’re just scratches.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:53.050
Lord, this old man has really become a thug in no time.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.220
What’s wrong, Kawachi?

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.800
You seem pale.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.220
N-Not really, Boss!

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.390
That’s not it!

00:03:58.390 --> 00:03:59.350
I mean Manager!

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.550
What in the world is that Roumen style?

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.600
Is it something really awesome?

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.980
That’s right, really awesome!

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:10.190
The Roumen style is a secret technique that has
been passed down from ancient times in China.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.860
First, you make one dough.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.530
A quarter of that dough is
preserved separately and not eaten.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:19.120
Then, the next time you make a new dough,
you add in the dough you’ve preserved.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.400
Next, you save one-fourth
of this new dough

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.700
and once again mix it into your next new dough.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:31.210
This technique involves repeating this process
indefinitely, slowly improving your dough.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.220
If you do this,

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.090
you get a dough that doesn’t lose in lightness to dough made with baking powder,

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.140
and that also has the
elasticity of dough made with yeast.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:42.300
An ultimate dough with a deep flavor will be born!

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:43.850
B-But...

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.310
A dough that takes such a
ridiculously long time to make...

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.300
When did Azuma start making it?

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.560
Azuma is young, but...

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:54.070
He’s a man who has been experimenting
with making <i>Japan</i> since childhood.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.240
So, he’s probably preserved some
dough by some method all these years.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.370
Oh, is that so?!

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.490
Azuma Kazuma... What a man...

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:07.000
His immensity always exceeds my imagination.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.880
However, no matter how awesome he is,

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.460
he can’t compare to Panda-chan’s steamed bread that explodes over and over again.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.510
Wh-What did you just say?!

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.510
What did you say, Mizuno?!

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:25.270
P-Panda-chan’s steamed bread
that explodes over and over again...?

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.980
How can that be?!

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:29.480
Did he finally complete it?

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:30.480
“It”?

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.110
Yeah...

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:36.070
This goes back to when we were
still young and happening newcomers...

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:42.900
One day, while we were drinking at a mixer for newcomers from various companies...

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:46.160
Say, since we’re all here like this...

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.910
Tell me what your dream as a baker is.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.040
I want to create the ultimate chocolate bread.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.290
I’m gonna be laying my life down for curry bread.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.920
I want to create Japan’s #1 French bread.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.590
So, what’s your dream?

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.640
My dream is...

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:12.560
to create a steamed bread that explodes
over and over again, like a Hollywood movie.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.860
That’s how he answered, but...

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.740
What? What? What is it?

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:23.410
Whoa, whoa.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:26.160
That’s just plain impossible to make, isn’t it?

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.370
Like a balloon, once it’s broken,
it can’t break again.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.660
I mean, think about it a little.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.840
His frustrated face...

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.590
I still remember it.

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:40.010
Is that so...?

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:42.460
Poor Panda-chan...

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.400
Back then, just like everyone else,

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.970
I thought that a bread like that really couldn’t be made, but...

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.640
Now that it’s made,

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.700
I guess he must’ve had a plan for making the ultimate steamed bread

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.440
ever since we were newcomers.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.480
I’m once again reminded of how fearsome a baker he is.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:02.980
At this rate... Azuma might lose again this time.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:03.980
What was that?!

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.410
I-It’s true!

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.740
There were three explosions!

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.040
It’s done.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.590
Th-That’s Mokoyama’s...

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:18.540
steamed bread that explodes over and over again, huh?

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:22.550
Judge, try it please.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.430
This is my dream, the Triple Alps Steamed Bread.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:32.180
Th-That steamed bread looks really soft.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.900
Since it exploded three times,

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.900
both the size and the number of the mountains
are completely different from regular Alps bread.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:43.320
From the looks of the progress during the baking
process, I was expecting this to be of high quality,

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.910
but to think it’d be like this...

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:48.910
This really requires me
to steel myself firmly.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.580
Come, try some.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:52.200
Before it gets cold.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:53.910
Yeah, sorry about that.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.170
Well, then.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:12.400
Until now, whenever he seemed to show no reaction at all,

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.480
it usually meant something was there, but...

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:17.300
This time there really doesn’t seem to be anything.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.730
I don’t sense anything.

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:24.740
P-Panda-chan...

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:26.740
What’s that?

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:29.570
What’s this sound that’s been ringing for a while?

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.910
Well, cheer up, Mizuno.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:34.960
Even if Azuma should win,
he won’t make fun of Panda.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.830
I’m sure that once the match
is over, they can be friends...

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:41.630
Oh no!

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:42.710
Everyone, down!

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:43.540
What was that?!

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:45.540
What?

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:49.680
Never mind that, get down!

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.270
The Panda’s bread is an awesome bread!

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.980
It’s just explosive!

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:01.810
It’s a good bread...

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.570
Kuro-yan exploded three times, and
has been blown into a million tiny pieces!

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.870
What a moron.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:21.000
Kuro-yan... You died for a stupid bread?

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.000
A true moron.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.010
A moron among morons!

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:26.880
The King of Morons!

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.890
You’re the moron.

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:31.010
Who’s that?

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.520
It’s mini Kuro-yans!

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.020
And, so many of them!

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:43.820
The guy who exploded into a million tiny
pieces was a robot put there in my place.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.030
Kuro-yan X.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:48.110
And these are my cute little servants.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:49.280
Gekimaru Kuro-yans.
Note: Gekimaru (<b>夏鬼丸): An anime about a robot.</b>

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:49.530
Note: Gekimaru (<b>夏鬼丸): An anime about a robot.</b>

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:50.780
Huh?
Note: Gekimaru (<b>夏鬼丸): An anime about a robot.</b>

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:53.030
I was pretending to show a reaction.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:55.490
During that time,
I secretly swapped my body on stage.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:58.750
It looks like you’ve become good at this.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:01.710
To express my appreciation for Panda’s magical bread,

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:04.420
where the same bread exploded up to three times,

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:07.010
I used magic as well.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.260
W-Well, that’s all very nice,

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.930
but where in the world is the real you?

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:16.720
Probably <i>there</i>.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.520
But, why... on the top of a mountain?

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:26.860
Probably because the “Alps” of
“Alps steamed bread” are mountains.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:27.400
That’s right!

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.850
Congratulations on figuring it out.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:30.900
Well then, let’s descend.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:31.780
Huh?

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:37.700
He really is a moron for doing
such an exaggerated reaction.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.160
Who you calling a moron?!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:39.870
That was quick!

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.960
That was a wonderful bread, Panda!

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:45.460
Not even I have ever seen

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:49.050
a bread where differences of temperature within
the dough have been manipulated so skillfully.

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:50.920
As expected of Kuroyanagi, the judge.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:54.140
He figured out the trick of
temperature difference just by eating it.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.050
I see...

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:57.100
That’s what it is...

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:58.430
Temperature difference?

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:00.060
That’s right.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:02.890
Just like a balloon,

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:06.730
once the dough of a steamed bread has exploded
once, it cannot explode a second or third time.

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:09.690
But, that’s only if there isn’t a
difference of temperatures within the dough.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:12.360
If you can maintain a difference
in temperature inside the dough,

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.570
it is possible to make any number of explosions.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:19.080
First, the portion that warms up first explodes.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.580
Then the portion to warm up next explodes.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.290
And the portion that warms up last explodes.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:29.800
Thus, you can have multiple
explosions over a period of time.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:32.420
B-But... wait, Kuro-yan!

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.800
While you say that you can maintain a
temperature difference within the dough...

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:39.260
Before you warm it, the dough for
the steamed bread is in a liquid state!

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:42.680
So, if you make a certain portion
cold, all of it will become cold,

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:46.440
and if you heat a certain portion,
it’s obvious that all of it will be heated.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.070
So how could you possibly
maintain a temperature difference!

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:52.070
You really are a moron, Kawachi.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.030
What was that?!

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:54.490
Think carefully.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:56.820
It’s true that the dough of
steamed bread is in liquid form.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.240
But, in addition to steamed bread,
what was the theme this time?

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.490
Theme...?

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.460
Umm... Chestnut kinton?

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:04.750
That’s right!

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:07.960
The chestnut kinton is the key player
in creating the temperature difference!

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:13.670
Panda probably cooled down the chestnut
kinton to freezing point and used it as a bridge

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.050
between the left and right regions.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:16.510
He placed it within the liquid,

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.350
and set it up so that when it was warmed,

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.520
the portions that weren’t
different temperatures would explode.

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.300
Is that how it is?!

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:30.810
By doing that, you can create a dough that is many times softer than regular doughs.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.860
Wh-What an out-of-this-world strategy.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.650
With something like this having been presented first,

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.080
Azuma can’t possibly have any hope of winning!

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.950
How’s that, Azuma-kun?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:47.080
In honor of the respect I have for your talent and skill,

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.210
this is a challenge I lay out before you.

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:53.090
Your Roumen-technique dough is great, but...

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:57.680
It cannot possibly match my Triple Alps Steamed Bread.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:00.930
You really are amazing,
Old Man Mokoyama.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.020
But, I ain’t gonna be losing, either.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:13.110
I... I smell something.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.400
What <i>is</i> this fragrance?

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:19.070
For some reason, it’s pulling me in.

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:21.370
A truly lovely fragrance.

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:24.660
A bold fragrance; the kind that
makes you think of roots flourishing in soil.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.610
Th-This is...!

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:34.340
Bamboo!

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:35.380
That’s right!

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:35.920
It’s bamboo!

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.390
You came with the Triple Alps,
right Old Man Mokoyama?

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:42.430
Well then...

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:45.430
I’m gonna meet you with
my Triple Bamboo!

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:47.930
Tr... Triple Bamboo?!

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:02.240
Here, Old Man...
I mean Mister Kuroyanagi.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.580
Please try it.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:08.040
I understood up until
the Roumen technique,

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.580
but Triple Bamboo, huh?

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:14.290
From the fragrance, it’s obvious
that bamboo has some relevance,

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.460
but what is this “triple” bit?

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:21.680
I hope that it isn’t something as stupid
as three twigs of bamboo inside, Azuma.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.350
Let’s go.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.570
He’s gone quiet again.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:40.240
We’ve been having a lot of this kind of reaction lately.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:41.700
No, that’s not it!

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:42.490
Please look!

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:45.740
Azuma-san already looks strange!

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.420
Th-That’s...

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.210
Roumen...

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.500
No, it’s a Noh mask!

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.170
Kuro-yan’s face has become a Roumen...

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.420
I mean a Noh mask!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.800
Th-That’s really creepy!

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.810
A man’s life of fifty years under the sky,

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:12.300
when compared to the age of this world...

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:15.770
And... He seems to be singing and dancing...

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:21.770
Is it anything more than a
fleeting dream or an illusion...?

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:28.030
Oh... Oh, no!

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:28.780
What is it this time?!

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:33.710
This is a stanza from the warrior hymn
“Atsumori” that Oda Nobunaga liked.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.420
Warrior hymn? “Atsumori”?

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:39.800
Put simply, the song says that
a man’s life is a mere fifty years.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:42.340
All who are born must die.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:46.930
If means that if you’re gonna die anyway,
then live your life short, but big.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:49.720
The reason that Nobunaga sang this before
setting out on the Battle of Okehazama is

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.850
because he thought that if he was
gonna live only fifty years anyway,

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:56.680
then he’d rather bet everything on
this one battle and die if necessary.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.190
So, what about it?!

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:00.190
In other words...

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.020
He’s...

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:04.910
laying everything down on this reaction,

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:06.530
and is ready to die if necessary!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.030
What was that?!

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:26.130
What is he planning to do?!

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:32.470
K-Kuro-yan?!

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:33.640
Oh, that is...?!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:42.030
What an anticlimax... He was
only pierced by bamboo sticks?

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:42.860
Looks like it.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:46.780
Moron! You can’t possibly judge in that state!

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:49.740
The only moron here is you, Kawachi.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:53.780
As if I would abandon the
judging, over something like this!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.580
Wh-What tenacity...

00:16:56.580 --> 00:17:00.250
Just what you’d expect of someone
who lays down his life on judging bread.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.800
Y-You think so...?

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:03.500
Azuma Kazuma.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:05.260
Wh-What is it?

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:09.180
A truly deeply mellow fragrance and faint sweetness.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.250
I, Kuroyanagi, stand in awe.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:15.480
You guys added bamboo tea instead of water, right?

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:16.690
That’s right!

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:21.400
Normally, people only think of bamboo leaves
as being used to wrap sushi and dumplings...

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.080
However, once they’ve been dried,

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:26.660
if you grind them up and make tea from them, it’s really delicious.

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:27.860
Yes.

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.610
But, how exactly
did you make this into tea?

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:34.610
I get the feeling that it’s somehow
different from regular bamboo tea.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.610
We boiled it in hot spring water.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.830
Oh, in hot spring water?

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:40.750
Well, it’s a hot spring bread, after all,

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:43.500
so it’s obvious that it’d be more
delicious if boiled in hot spring water.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:48.010
And, we made sure to add bamboo leaves
into the water we used to steam the bread, too.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:52.140
So, the fragrance should be perfect.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:53.640
I see.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:57.020
The taste of bamboo tea, and
the fragrance of bamboo leaves...

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:59.730
These are two of the strategies you applied, right?

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:03.900
So, what’s the third strategy?

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.280
Since you call it Triple Bamboo,
there should be one more, right?

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.450
That, you see...

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.110
is your blood!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.860
I... I see, the health benefit!

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:16.660
Bamboo is called the green blood...

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:22.220
It is a great natural health product
that helps your blood flow more smoothly.

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:27.760
I was thinking that for some
reason I can’t stop bleeding.

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:30.470
I guess that my blood flow is a little too smooth...

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:33.220
Looks like it.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:35.260
L-Looks like that was...

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.680
Blood, huh?

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:41.890
Victor: Pantasia!

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:43.100
All right!

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:44.850
We did it!

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.850
Yeah, we did!

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:51.070
W-Wait a minute, Kuro-yan!

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:51.780
What is it?

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:53.530
I admit that the Roumen technique was superb.

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:55.990
But it’s just the bamboo that’s great, right?

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.740
In terms of skill,
isn’t the Triple Alps better?

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:02.370
That might be true.

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:03.580
But...

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.170
K-Kuro-yan!

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.710
You look really pale!

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.260
Are you gonna die?!

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:11.930
So, what is it?

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:12.970
Explain it to us!

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:17.850
It didn’t go well with the chestnut kinton, Boss.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.520
Panda-chan!

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:24.350
The softness of my steamed
bread is in the realm of cakes.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.440
So, it goes well with
Western-style ingredients,

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:28.440
but it doesn’t complement
Japanese-style ingredients well.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.070
If I were to make it complement the
chestnut kinton, which is Japanese,

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.820
I would have made the dough
a little stickier.

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:35.320
No way...

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:38.650
And, Azuma-kun’s Roumen dough,

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:42.210
having been fermented for a really long time, is very sticky.

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:44.710
Also, the bamboo tea goes
well with the chestnut kinton.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:46.330
So, it’s obvious that I’d lose.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.000
But why, Panda-chan?!

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:52.880
If you knew about that weakness,
why didn’t you work on fixing it?

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:53.460
Why?!

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:56.920
It’s not as if I noticed it
from the beginning.

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:02.520
Before the match, all that I could
think of was beating Azuma-kun.

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:07.300
I didn’t have the composure I needed to judge
the strengths and weaknesses of my bread.

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:09.780
But, now I know...

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:14.530
both my personal foolishness,
and the foolishness of human beings.

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:15.030
Okay?

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:17.070
The foolishness of human beings?

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:20.080
Yeah, because now, I have...

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.750
become a real panda!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.130
What?!

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:30.580
What was that?!

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:36.960
It’s just that my body automatically
reacted to that mellow fragrance.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:40.220
Wh-What a complicated reaction...

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:45.850
Hey! Are you all right, old man?!

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:47.520
Yeah, I’m fine.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:50.150
And surprisingly, I kinda feel refreshed.

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:55.150
In the end, any battle is a battle with yourself.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:57.490
I didn’t know that.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.910
Unlike me, who only cared about wins and losses,

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.290
so much that I entered the match
ignoring my Boss’s objections...

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:08.210
all you do is try and improve your own bread, not caring about who the opponent is.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:11.550
It’s inevitable that you should win.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:13.210
Old man...

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:16.090
Let’s go, Boss.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:18.140
Hop onto my back.

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:28.020
Thank you, Azuma-kun.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.860
I learned a lot from you again.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:31.570
See ya.

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:33.150
Bye bye, Kazu-kun.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:35.860
O-Old man...

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:42.370
I wonder if the old man will be all right...

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:46.830
Now that he’s a panda, he can’t even board trains.

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:49.790
He’ll be fine,
even if he can’t board trains.

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:52.670
He can walk with his own feet now.

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:56.210
His battle with you has helped him mature once again.

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:58.340
I see...

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:03.760
That’s right.

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:05.340
Yep.

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:08.480
Then, all’s well that ends well, right?

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:17.320
You’ve been forgotten, Kuro-yan.

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:18.490
Yeah...

00:22:18.490 --> 00:22:22.120
Now that I think about it,
I don’t wanna die.

00:22:22.120 --> 00:22:24.280
Kawachi... An ambulance...

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:25.660
I’m a moron...

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:27.450
I don’t know how to call an ambulance.

00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:29.750
Please, Kawachi-kun...

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:31.710
I can’t hear you.

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:34.130
Meanie.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:44.090
Robbie, come on out to the sound of the voice calling you.

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:52.010
Robbie, you were crying all by yourself.

00:22:52.180 --> 00:23:00.350
Robbie, the eyes in your heart...

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:03.820
what is it that they reflect?

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:07.240
...Is it “Who am I?”...

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:15.030
The other side of the mirage flickers faintly.

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:23.630
Anywhere is fine, as long as it’s not here.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:32.340
My dancing heart is reborn as a marble time and again.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:36.470
The colors I just filled in were yours.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:40.390
It’s not something that will finish with a turn. Be load.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:48.320
Just like your joy, try letting your tears flow.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:52.410
See? The world is filled in with your colors.

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:59.080
Like a tumble, do the best of you.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:06.880
He became a real panda!

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:08.090
For real, anything goes here, huh?

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:09.510
Don’t be spacing out.

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:11.680
There’s only two more matches in Yakitate!! 9!

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:12.350
That’s right!

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:13.810
So, our next opponent is...

00:24:13.810 --> 00:24:15.060
Huh? What was that?!

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:16.310
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.310 --> 00:24:17.520
The sun vs. the blizzard!!

00:24:17.520 --> 00:24:18.940
The ultimate tart showdown!

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate Seeds of Knowledge!!

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:26.480
Bamboo-leaf dumplings, cakes, and sushi all use "beargrass."

00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:29.470
In addition to outstanding taste, it brings chlorophyll and flavonoids to the table.

00:24:29.470 --> 00:24:31.770
It's chock-full of nutritious goodness!

00:24:32.160 --> 00:24:34.550
Ehhhhh!??!!
